'' A literal past 64 bits is fbc's warning 8, "Literal number too big, truncated" -- decimal
'' and '&h' alike, measured on lines 1, 2 and 4 here; the all-ones value was already fbc's.
'' TKO0205 had a message and no emitter, one of eight such ids; the other seven are gone
'' (audit F-67).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -c tests/diagnostics/src/literal-too-big.bas -o tests/diagnostics/src/literal-too-big.o
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: literal-too-big.bas(1,7): warning TKO0205
'' EXPECT-OUT: literal-too-big.bas(2,7): warning TKO0205
'' EXPECT-OUT: literal-too-big.bas(4,7): warning TKO0205
'' EXPECT-NOT: (3,7): warning
'' EXPECT-NOT: (5,7): warning
